Reference palettes

The Atari standard NTSC and SECAM RGB tables are adapted from Stella:
Copyright (c) 1995-2026 Bradford W. Mott, Stephen Anthony and the Stella Team.
Stella permits use under the GNU GPL version 2 or any later version. The
adapted data is distributed with PixelC3 under GPL version 3 or later.
The NTSC table omits the unused placeholder entries from the Stella source.

Source: https://github.com/stella-emu/stella/blob/master/src/common/PaletteHandler.cxx
License notice: https://github.com/stella-emu/stella/blob/master/Copyright.txt

Apple II NTSC RGB values: Robert Munafo's published color calculations.
C64 PAL colors: independent implementation of Philip 'Pepto' Timmermann's
Colodore reference model and documented default display settings.
NES RGB DAC values: NESdev's documented 2C03/2C05 palette table.
Further sources and representation limits are documented in
docs/PALETTE_REFERENCES.md.

Processing references

Oklab conversion uses Björn Ottosson's published transform.
https://bottosson.github.io/posts/oklab/

Overlay and Soft Light follow W3C Compositing and Blending Level 1.
https://www.w3.org/TR/compositing-1/#blendingseparable
